From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:30:00 -0300
Subject: Wayland: a stereo window says the size one of its views is shown at

A program that renders each eye at a resolution of its own (a render
resolution per eye setting) keeps that resolution in the window's
buffer and lets the compositor do the one resize: Stereo KWin shows a
declared surface at its wp_viewport destination, whatever the buffer's
size (kde_stereo_content_v1 version 2: the viewport destination is the
size of one view). The window may now say that size with the dynamic
property _q_stereo_view_size (a QSize in logical pixels); its viewport
destination is then that size, whatever its geometry, for a window the
display stack packs (a stereo surface format) and for one that holds
its views side by side alike. Windows without the property are
unchanged.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.1
Index: src/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/qwaylandwindow.cpp
===================================================================
--- src.orig/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/qwaylandwindow.cpp
+++ src/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/qwaylandwindow.cpp
@@ -572,6 +572,12 @@ void QWaylandWindow::updateViewport()
     const int views = window()->property("_q_stereo_side_by_side_views").toInt();
     if (views > 1)
         destination.setWidth(destination.width() / views);
+    // A stereo window may render its views at a resolution of its own and say the size one view is shown
+    // at (_q_stereo_view_size, in logical pixels): its buffer keeps the render resolution and the
+    // compositor does the one resize.
+    const QSize viewSize = window()->property("_q_stereo_view_size").toSize();
+    if (viewSize.isValid() && !viewSize.isEmpty())
+        destination = viewSize;
     if (!destination.isEmpty())
         mViewport->setDestination(destination);
 }
